WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.207 --> 00:00:01.636
- The only thing I know about Peru

00:00:01.636 --> 00:00:04.153
has to do with llamas and alpacas,

00:00:04.153 --> 00:00:05.745
but I really hope you don't eat them

00:00:05.745 --> 00:00:07.505
because they're so cute.

00:00:10.398 --> 00:00:11.968
- [Man] All of our
knowledge of Peruvian food

00:00:11.968 --> 00:00:14.204
is based off of The Emperor's New Groove.

00:00:14.204 --> 00:00:15.815
- My dad went to Peru once.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.149
I love pieces of beef.

00:00:23.149 --> 00:00:24.237
- Wait, is this llama?

00:00:24.237 --> 00:00:26.008
- If this was what the steak
at Chipotle tasted like,

00:00:26.008 --> 00:00:28.210
I'd be ordering steak burritos
instead of chicken burritos.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.300
- I like the veggies.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.750
- Ooh, what veggies?

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:31.979
- Look at the veggies.

00:00:31.979 --> 00:00:33.754
- You wanna eat onions and the fries?

00:00:33.754 --> 00:00:34.620
- I would eat those.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:35.386
- All the time.

00:00:35.386 --> 00:00:36.393
- Breakfast, lunch and dinner.

00:00:36.393 --> 00:00:38.258
- Maybe not that, but
I'd eat it a lot, yeah.

00:00:38.258 --> 00:00:39.898
- It's like a llama.

00:00:39.898 --> 00:00:40.829
- No, it's beef.

00:00:42.099 --> 00:00:44.014
- You don't know that, maybe
a llama's made out of beef.

00:00:44.014 --> 00:00:45.845
- No, it's not, I do know

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.351
that a llama's not made out of beef.

00:00:47.351 --> 00:00:48.679
- Have you ever eaten a llama?

00:00:48.679 --> 00:00:49.615
- No.

00:00:53.575 --> 00:00:55.131
- [Man] This looks like it could have been

00:00:55.131 --> 00:00:56.780
from The Emperor's New Groove.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:58.602
- I'm gonna make a bet that
we're not gonna like this.

00:00:58.602 --> 00:00:59.305
- Ooh.

00:00:59.305 --> 00:01:00.400
- We could draw our names in it.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.164
- I was immediately going to write Keith,

00:01:02.164 --> 00:01:03.212
are you writing Kelsey?

00:01:03.212 --> 00:01:05.182
- The sauce, it lingers, like,

00:01:05.182 --> 00:01:07.066
I can't get it out of my mouth.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:09.159
- It probably tastes
like scalloped potato.

00:01:09.159 --> 00:01:10.227
- You know that scene in Hook?

00:01:10.227 --> 00:01:12.276
Where they, all the kids,
they're playing imaginary

00:01:12.276 --> 00:01:13.339
with the food.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.030
This looks like some stuff out of that.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.801
- You always think that that
food's gonna be delicious.

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:18.373
- Yeah, because it's like ice cream.

00:01:18.373 --> 00:01:19.973
But this is not ice cream.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.790
- [Man] I feel like a witch made this.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:27.222
I feel like someone was
like, "Ah, the leg of a crab.

00:01:27.222 --> 00:01:28.734
"The tentacle of a squid."

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:31.497
- Yeah, this is finally going
to make that girl I like

00:01:31.497 --> 00:01:32.604
fall in love with me.

00:01:32.604 --> 00:01:34.093
- The thing I like about this soup.

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:35.957
(she laughs)

00:01:35.957 --> 00:01:36.993
Actually, it's not that bad.

00:01:36.993 --> 00:01:38.380
- No, it's good, but it's like,

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:41.420
everything from the ocean is in this bowl.

00:01:42.791 --> 00:01:43.840
- God, it's terrible.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:47.305
- It tastes like the ocean tastes.

00:01:47.305 --> 00:01:49.436
But deliciouser.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.470
- Smells good, looks good.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:58.470
- This looks like something
you should have at Halloween.

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:01.969
- It's lighten than jam but
it's thicker than jello.

00:02:01.969 --> 00:02:04.068
- I'm thinking about the same rhyme.

00:02:04.068 --> 00:02:06.685
- But when it gets in my
mouth, I say, "Hello!"

00:02:06.685 --> 00:02:08.121
- Hello!

00:02:08.121 --> 00:02:09.386
- Kind of reminds me of the thing

00:02:09.386 --> 00:02:12.387
you rub on women's bellies
when they get an ultrasound.

00:02:12.387 --> 00:02:13.918
- Like petrolium jelly?

00:02:13.918 --> 00:02:16.488
- I think kids would
love this, because like,

00:02:16.488 --> 00:02:18.280
it's purple, that's fun.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.154
It's got fruit in it, fruit's awesome,

00:02:20.154 --> 00:02:22.005
and it's like sugary,
cinnamony, it's great.

00:02:23.044 --> 00:02:25.395
- [Man] Started off really
strong with the beef dish,

00:02:25.395 --> 00:02:26.252
loved that.

00:02:26.252 --> 00:02:27.187
- Remember the beef dish?

00:02:27.187 --> 00:02:28.088
- I miss it.

00:02:28.088 --> 00:02:30.102
- It was good, it's like,
some of it was really eclectic

00:02:30.102 --> 00:02:32.378
which is interesting, and
some of it was really simple.

00:02:32.378 --> 00:02:35.300
- Overall, Peru, yeah you
got food people can eat,

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.768
and the seafood is pretty
good, the corn stuff is fine,

00:02:37.768 --> 00:02:40.697
the potatoes were confusing,
but overall, I'd eat it.

00:02:41.776 --> 00:02:43.122
- I'll give you a solid--

00:02:43.122 --> 00:02:45.176
- I'd give it at least a 45.

00:02:45.176 --> 00:02:47.453
- Can you see my llama pants?

00:02:47.453 --> 00:02:49.275
It it possible to see them?

00:02:49.275 --> 00:02:50.958
- You should just, like, lay on the table.

00:02:50.958 --> 00:02:51.931
- These are party llamas,

00:02:51.931 --> 00:02:53.846
it's why they are dressed in colors.

00:02:55.468 --> 00:02:57.462
- It's just so sad what's
happening over there.

00:02:57.462 --> 00:02:58.779
- Oh, yeah.

00:03:01.652 --> 00:03:03.212
You don't know the half of it.

